{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers","id":1446429,"title":"[\u00c6on] Stalwarts in \u00c6on Trinity and Superior Powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-29T03:49:03-07:00","id":1446429,"title":"[\u00c6on] Stalwarts in \u00c6on Trinity and Superior Powers","content":"I have a few questions about Stalwarts (from Adventure! setting):<br /> 1 - Its possible they exist in \u00c6on Trinity era?<br /> 2 - Can use BioApps?<br /> 3 - They are detect as Novas/Quantum users?<br /> <br /> Now about Superiors:<br /> 1 - In the future there will be more superior powers in official books?<br /> 2 - I saw some similarities between the Superiors powers and Stalwarts' gifts, it's possible to &quot;convert&quot; these gifts into Superiors powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T04:02:39-07:00","id":1446431,"title":"","content":"Stalwarts<br /> 1- No, Stalwarts are a interaction of a low powered Nova and the Doyen Shield around Earth. They existed only between Hammersmith and N-Day.<br /> <br /> 2- Probably yes, because like Superiors, the power is not that much to damage it immediately, BUT they probably damage it in the long run.<br /> <br /> 3- Probably yes, but Novas and Quantum Sensors are not available when they are... Psions probably sense them as very week non corrupted Novas, different from Superiors somehow, but they are more powerful than superiors.<br /> <br /> Superiors<br /> 1- Doubt, but...<br /> <br /> 2- Personal opinion here, but it\u2019s far easier to just use Stalwart to simulate Superiors, and cut the DE from the list of possibilities. Converting Gifts in powers would be hardwork and may not work as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T04:05:36-07:00","id":1446432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers#post1446429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few questions about Stalwarts (from Adventure! setting):<br /> 1 - Its possible they exist in \u00c6on Trinity era?<br /> 2 - Can use BioApps?<br /> 3 - They are detect as Novas/Quantum users?</div> </div> </div> </div>Answers are heavily caveated with \u2018do what works for your game\u2019, of course, but from the view of the setting as published:<br /> <br /> 1 - Unlikely. Quantum Flux and Corruption are too available for Quantum paths to stop at the lower Stalwart levels.<br /> 2 - Probably.<br /> 3 - Probably not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now about Superiors:<br /> 1 - In the future there will be more superior powers in official books?<br /> 2 - I saw some similarities between the Superiors powers and Stalwarts' gifts, it's possible to convert these gifts into Superiors powers? </div> </div> </div>1 - Impossible to say until future books are published.<br /> 2 - If you want to do so, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T19:46:37-07:00","id":1446545,"title":"","content":"More Superior powers sounds like an ideal topic for a Storypath Nexus book if anyone wants to make one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T02:41:16-07:00","id":1446575,"title":"","content":"Random but really important question<br /> <br /> If the Doyen Shield exists around Earth between the Hammersmith event and N-Day, does that mean there are stalwarts and mesmerists in the core setting (as well as Talents)? If so, can they still use Dramatic Editing?<br /> <br /> Thanks \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T03:22:39-07:00","id":1446579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1446575#post1446575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random but really important question<br /> <br /> If the Doyen Shield exists around Earth between the Hammersmith event and N-Day, does that mean there are stalwarts and mesmerists in the core setting (as well as Talents)? If so, can they still use Dramatic Editing?<br /> <br /> Thanks \ud83d\ude0a</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, a very small number of each, less than the number of Talents.<br /> <br /> I would not allow them to Dramatic Editing, for the same reason Talents don\u2019t have the same Dramatic Editing advantages anymore (using Momentum to DE), as the general flux level was reduced, the exception is the special DE allowed only to Stalwarts and Mesmerists (mini max out and mini reach). It probably compensate the reduced DE capacities from Talents in core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T08:04:23-07:00","id":1446603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1446575#post1446575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random but really important question<br /> <br /> If the Doyen Shield exists around Earth between the Hammersmith event and N-Day, does that mean there are stalwarts and mesmerists in the core setting (as well as Talents)? If so, can they still use Dramatic Editing?<br /> <br /> Thanks \ud83d\ude0a</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that they're still around; but they've become rare. This is due to the ambient energies fading away over time. As for Dramatic Editing: I'm unsure. The fasting away of the telluric energies has left the Talents without the Dramatic Editing discount that the daredevils had during the Adventure era; it's possible that the ability of stalwarts and mesmerists to engage in similar Dramatic Editing has all but disappeared; or it may still be around, at the same +1 Inspiration cost (or possibly even higher). What they should definitely keep are their own unique forms of Dramatic Editing (the ability to change up their Psychic Gifts in the case of mesmerists, and the ability to exceed their limits in the case of stalwarts). <br /> <br /> If another Event takes place while the Doyen barrier is up, you get a resurgence of the Adventure era, but on a smaller scale: more localized, and a shorter duration. But where it happens and while it lasts, you get a boom: if it's a Hammersmith-style Event, you get a resurgence of daredevils, stalwarts, and mesmerists; if it's a precursor to Divas Mal's Event, you get a return of stalwarts, possibly with some sort of upgrade making them a bit more like Novas; and if you get a precursor to SK's Event, you get a return of mesmerists, possibly with some sort of upgrade making them a bit more like psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:20:23-07:00","id":1446624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1446603#post1446603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If another Event takes place while the Doyen barrier is up, you get a resurgence of the Adventure era, but on a smaller scale: more localized, and a shorter duration. But where it happens and while it lasts, you get a boom: if it's a Hammersmith-style Event, you get a resurgence of daredevils, stalwarts, and mesmerists; if it's a precursor to Divas Mal's Event, you get a return of stalwarts, possibly with some sort of upgrade making them a bit more like Novas; and if you get a precursor to SK's Event, you get a return of mesmerists, possibly with some sort of upgrade making them a bit more like psiads.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a fan of this sort of kick off to a modern game. All kinds of wild attempts to create weapons and otherwise tinker with weird science (real or unreal) come to mind. The Philadelphia Experiment, CERN, the Stargate Project, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T14:28:10-07:00","id":1446658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers#post1446429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few questions about Stalwarts (from Adventure! setting):<br /> 1 - Its possible they exist in \u00c6on Trinity era?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - Not naturally, as noted several times above. If you really want stalwarts to exist in \u00c6on, you'll need an appropriate MacGuffin. Maybe some Aberrant War era nova wanted to protect the human populace of their town from others of his kind, so built a device to generate a quantum energy suppression zone (avoiding the worst of the effect themself by generally staying inside the 'eye' of the effect or just dorming down to interact with the townsfolk).<br /> <br /> The device's creator transcended years ago, so the thing is slowly breaking down without proper maintenance; sending out jolts of quantum energy immediately followed by a renewed suppressive effect. This results in people walking near the device occasionally turning into stalwarts.<br /> <br /> One the one hand, the proper way to handle inexplicable quantum tech is to haul it off and destroy it. On the other hand, a device that suppresses nova powers over an area the size of a town is priceless. On the - most worrying - third hand, the device either failing or being removed may result in the town's stalwarts turning into novas, who then risk turning into aberrants.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:44:51-07:00","id":1446699,"title":"","content":"My head canon is that the Galatea event in 2018 created a split in the timeline, with one divergent timeline becoming the TC core setting and Assassins and the other one becoming Aberrant, Anima and Aeon. What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T20:31:25-07:00","id":1446724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1446699#post1446699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My head canon is that the Galatea event in 2018 created a split in the timeline, with one divergent timeline becoming the TC core setting and Assassins and the other one becoming Aberrant, Anima and Aeon. What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me. And another timeline where a second Inspiration Age is created! Heck, the real 2018 was awash in so much craziness, Stalwarts and Mesmerists would be lost in the chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-30-2021, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T21:18:20-07:00","id":1446730,"title":"","content":"The manuscript for TC:Adventure! suggests that there was at least one alternate timeline where Michael didn't survive long enough to attempt the Galatea Event, and that that future ended up being dominated by Talents. My head canon is that <i>that's</i> the timeline of the core book and Assassins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T05:24:20-07:00","id":1446784,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Core being a parallel reality with Assassins, but I think the best place to put Core is in the 1970s to 2000s, when action heroes were the thing in the movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T07:35:21-07:00","id":1446794,"title":"","content":"Alternately, you could say that the 80s and 90s were an Adventure-style resurgence in the main timeline: basically, take the setting from the core book, transplant it into the last two centuries of the 20th century, and populate it with daredevils, stalwarts, and mesmerists instead of Talents. All you need is a triggering Event that's powerful enough to pump up the telluric energy levels to where they were in the 1930s, but without enough power to break the Doyen barrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T07:51:57-07:00","id":1446795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1446730#post1446730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The manuscript for TC:Adventure! suggests that there was at least one alternate timeline where Michael didn't survive long enough to attempt the Galatea Event, and that that future ended up being dominated by Talents. My head canon is that <i>that's</i> the timeline of the core book and Assassins.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense! I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T10:37:04-07:00","id":1446810,"title":"","content":"And there is the issue if Stalwarts are created they would be stable in an environment that has free quantum flux. From Primori's theory, all Stalwarts would be free to ascend (Aberrant-fashion) with a better environment (i.e., without the Doyen Shield).<br /> <br /> So, Superiors come with a lock to make them stuck at that level, Stalwarts do not. Maybe there could be a variation to the Superior Process to make stable Stalwarts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","user":"pcontop","date":". 05-01-2021, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:46:30-07:00","id":1446831,"title":"","content":"As I see, Superiors are stable and locked in level Stalwart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T14:45:42-07:00","id":1446850,"title":"","content":"Have you guys experimented with Superiors appearing before the late Aberrant period (I think I read in canon that the first Superiors were created in Nippon near the end of the Aberrant War)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T15:11:29-07:00","id":1446851,"title":"","content":"I think it was even before that, but there was too few and Nihon was already closed, so they didn\u2019t go too far.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s something you can change in your game. A Nova discover a way to erupt Novas but when they do they are locked in their power level. It could be anywhere in the world other than Japan with a good chance to spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T16:42:50-07:00","id":1447055,"title":"","content":"It has been mentioned that stalwarts are the way they are because the Doyen barrier altered the way that the telluric energies interact with each other and with the Inspired. If you <i>want</i> stalwarts in later eras, you could say that when and if the nature of Talents is discovered (remember: in-setting, most people believe that Talents are \u201cmerely\u201d extraordinarily fortunate, competent, and determined; <i>not</i> subconscious reality warpers), someone might engage in some investigation into how their \u201creality flux\u201d powers interact with the quantum and subquantum energies that are much better known in the \u00c6on era. And those investigations might come up with a variation of the process that Nihon uses to produce Superiors, which instead produces quantum-powered individuals capable of indirectly manipulating reality flux to a limited extent \u2014 that is, stalwarts. No Quantum Powers, Mega-Attributes, or Mega-Edges for them; not even Superior Powers; \u201cjust\u201d Dynamic Gifts. <br /> <br /> That is: barring another \u201cDoyen barrier\u201d scenario, <i>naturally occurring</i> stalwarts aren't going to happen, as any that do well end up Erupting as Novas; but it might be possible to <i>artificially induce and maintain</i> a stalwart, given the right knowledge of the \u201ctelluric energies\u201d involved. <br /> <br /> Or consider going with an alternate version of the \u00c6on setting, where Nihon's great innovation wasn't \u201ca process to create Superiors\u201d, but a more localized version of the Doyen barrier: <i>within the confines of their islands</i>, you get mesmerists instead of psiads and stalwarts instead of Novas, and Talents get all of the benefits that daredevils had in the Adventure era. In exchange, there's no such thing as a Superior; reports to that effect are actually references to the stalwarts of the island nation. <br /> <br /> Of course, if you do that, you'll also want to address what happens when a stalwart or mesmerist goes outside the shield; or what an Aberrant or psion goes <i>inside</i>. Maybe there <i>is</i> a Nakamura(?) Process; but rather than <i>creating</i> a Superior (which now becomes this variant setting's term for \u201cInspired in the style of Adventure\u201d), it merely <i>stabilizes</i> them, preventing them from Erupting into Aberrants or psiads when they depart the island. And conversely, it's \u201ctoo late\u201d for Aberrants, psions, and psiads: the genie is out of the bottle, as it were. So entering the barrier doesn't turn them into stalwarts and mesmerists; though it might make it harder for them to use their powers. <br /> <br /> Definitely not canon; but it might make for a fun alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T04:08:57-07:00","id":1447172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447055#post1447055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been mentioned that stalwarts are the way they are because the Doyen barrier altered the way that the telluric energies interact with each other and with the Inspired. If you <i>want</i> stalwarts in later eras, you could say that when and if the nature of Talents is discovered (remember: in-setting, most people believe that Talents are \u201cmerely\u201d extraordinarily fortunate, competent, and determined; <i>not</i> subconscious reality warpers), someone might engage in some investigation into how their \u201creality flux\u201d powers interact with the quantum and subquantum energies that are much better known in the \u00c6on era. And those investigations might come up with a variation of the process that Nihon uses to produce Superiors, which instead produces quantum-powered individuals capable of indirectly manipulating reality flux to a limited extent \u2014 that is, stalwarts. No Quantum Powers, Mega-Attributes, or Mega-Edges for them; not even Superior Powers; \u201cjust\u201d Dynamic Gifts.<br /> <br /> That is: barring another \u201cDoyen barrier\u201d scenario, <i>naturally occurring</i> stalwarts aren't going to happen, as any that do well end up Erupting as Novas; but it might be possible to <i>artificially induce and maintain</i> a stalwart, given the right knowledge of the \u201ctelluric energies\u201d involved.<br /> <br /> Or consider going with an alternate version of the \u00c6on setting, where Nihon's great innovation wasn't \u201ca process to create Superiors\u201d, but a more localized version of the Doyen barrier: <i>within the confines of their islands</i>, you get mesmerists instead of psiads and stalwarts instead of Novas, and Talents get all of the benefits that daredevils had in the Adventure era. In exchange, there's no such thing as a Superior; reports to that effect are actually references to the stalwarts of the island nation.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you do that, you'll also want to address what happens when a stalwart or mesmerist goes outside the shield; or what an Aberrant or psion goes <i>inside</i>. Maybe there <i>is</i> a Nakamura(?) Process; but rather than <i>creating</i> a Superior (which now becomes this variant setting's term for \u201cInspired in the style of Adventure\u201d), it merely <i>stabilizes</i> them, preventing them from Erupting into Aberrants or psiads when they depart the island. And conversely, it's \u201ctoo late\u201d for Aberrants, psions, and psiads: the genie is out of the bottle, as it were. So entering the barrier doesn't turn them into stalwarts and mesmerists; though it might make it harder for them to use their powers.<br /> <br /> Definitely not canon; but it might make for a fun alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Doyen created the barrier as a response to the Hammersmith event. Can you point me to where it says they put it up?<br /> <br /> And if I understand <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a> correctly, Stalwarts are novas and mesmercists are psiads; they use Talent like rules in Adventure because it is easier to model them that way. What with being put on the same tier and not having to reprint 300+ pages of rules and all.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of taking some of these 'special' Gifts and turning them into abilities available to Superiors (as additional power options) and Psions/Psiads (as psionic edges) though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 05-03-2021, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T04:23:10-07:00","id":1447174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447172#post1447172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the Doyen created the barrier as a response to the Hammersmith event. Can you point me to where it says they put it up?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1434232-tc-adventure-kickstarter?p=1444832#post1444832\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...32#post1444832</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if I understand IanWatsson correctly, Stalwarts are novas and mesmercists are psiads; they use Talent like rules in Adventure because it is easier to model them that way. What with being put on the same tier and not having to reprint 300+ pages of rules and all. </div> </div> </div>They are, but they have some limitations due to the Doyen Barrier.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would read them as regular Novas and Psiads using a different system to make it all easier (as you described), while the Dramatic Editing being from the fact there is so much Flux available that even non Talents can bend reality with some effort. But that\u2019s my take...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do like the idea of taking some of these 'special' Gifts and turning them into abilities available to Superiors (as additional power options) and Psions/Psiads (as psionic edges) though. </div> </div> </div>There is one book in the Nexus with many Psionic Edges that already brings many of those to Aeon, it\u2019s called Mind over Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-03-2021, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T05:05:45-07:00","id":1447178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447172#post1447172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Doyen created the barrier as a response to the Hammersmith event. Can you point me to where it says they put it up?</div> </div> </div> </div> It's in the setting secrets part of the TC:A! manuscript. There's also a post by one of the developers right near the end of the TC:A! Kickstarter thread where she spells it out explicitly; when I have more time, I'll dig up the link. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447172#post1447172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if I understand <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> correctly, Stalwarts are novas and mesmerists are psiads; they use Talent like rules in Adventure because it is easier to model them that way. What with being put on the same tier and not having to reprint 300+ pages of rules and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Close, but not quite. The presence of the Doyen barrier changed the way that the telluric energies interact with empowered humans. Some of this manifests as a limitation on how powerful stalwarts and mesmerists are compared to Novas and psiads; but it also manifests in mesmerist Gifts being all over the place compared even to psiad Aptitudes and Modes. But most significantly, it alters the relationship that those empowered by Quantum and Psi energies have with Dramatic Editing: without the effects of the Doyen barrier, Novas, psions, and psiads cannot engage in the reality-altering phenomenon called Dramatic Editing at all; <i>with</i> the barrier in place, they <i>can</i>; just not as effectively as Talents. <br /> <br /> Basically, the way it was described in the TC:A! Kickstarter thread was that it's <i>not</i> just a different set of game systems employed to represent exactly the same thing; the subtle differences that exist because of the different rules exist within the setting as well, and Michael and Sara manifest as a (powerful) stalwart and mesmerist, respectively, because the Doyen put up the barrier almost immediately and altered their relationship with Quantum and Psi, an effect that lasted until Michael broke the barrier on N Day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T06:59:20-07:00","id":1447187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447178#post1447178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) Michael and Sara manifest as a (powerful) stalwart and mesmerist, respectively, because the Doyen put up the barrier almost immediately and altered their relationship with Quantum and Psi, an effect that lasted until Michael broke the barrier on N Day.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This goes against Aberrant Canon, because C.Pax was a naturally erupted Nova before N-Day, and Divis Mal also (that's why he was powerful enough to break the barrier in the first place). If my memory is right, Scripture was also a pre-N-Day Nova.<br /> <br /> 2)This goes against Core Canon, because there were Talents in Core, but not Stalwarts and Mesmerists (and Daredevils if you consider them to be different from Core's Talents).<br /> <br /> How to reconcile all these?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T07:27:46-07:00","id":1447191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447187#post1447187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How to reconcile all these?</div> </div> </div> </div>Change canon for your game. There is a continuum of dimensions, and your game does not have to be explicitly placed on the one presented in the books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T07:29:03-07:00","id":1447192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447187#post1447187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) This goes against Aberrant Canon, because C.Pax was a naturally erupted Nova before N-Day, and Divis Mal also (that's why he was powerful enough to break the barrier in the first place). If my memory is right, Scripture was also a pre-N-Day Nova.<br /> <br /> 2)This goes against Core Canon, because there were Talents in Core, but not Stalwarts and Mesmerists (and Daredevils if you consider them to be different from Core's Talents).<br /> <br /> How to reconcile all these?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Not necessarily. Pax was described as a Nova because there was no better term to describe in the setting. Same for Mal and Sara, Mal was described as a Nova erupting in the 1920s, and Sara as a powerful psiad, but they were Stalwart and Mesmerist by the standards of the time. In the end a Stalwart is a Nova that was limited somehow.<br /> <br /> 2. There are Stalwarts and Mesmerists in Core, they are just not that active and that numerous. They probably lost the DE capacity when Hammersmith effects lowered over time, but they are still powered and present. Pax for example erupted during \u201ccore\u201d.<br /> <br /> By the way, during Aberrant era, Psiads would be called Novas, as well as more overt Talents. They would be Dark Stars (some one even said they are the ones called Dark Stars, because they are not detected by quantum sensors, but still have powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-03-2021, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T07:44:36-07:00","id":1447194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447187#post1447187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) This goes against Aberrant Canon, because C.Pax was a naturally erupted Nova before N-Day, and Divis Mal also (that's why he was powerful enough to break the barrier in the first place). If my memory is right, Scripture was also a pre-N-Day Nova.<br /> <br /> 2)This goes against Core Canon, because there were Talents in Core, but not Stalwarts and Mesmerists (and Daredevils if you consider them to be different from Core's Talents).<br /> <br /> How to reconcile all these?</div> </div> </div> </div>Story-wise, I would just say that it is different names for the same types of Supernormal beings. And as far as power level goes, Stalwarts with enough xp, Dramatic Editing and Super Science devices, can be immensely powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T07:48:24-07:00","id":1447197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447192#post1447192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Not necessarily. Pax was described as a Nova because there was no better term to describe in the setting. Same for Mal and Sara, Mal was described as a Nova erupting in the 1920s, and Sara as a powerful psiad, but they were Stalwart and Mesmerist by the standards of the time. In the end a Stalwart is a Nova that was limited somehow.<br /> <br /> 2. There are Stalwarts and Mesmerists in Core, they are just not that active and that numerous. They probably lost the DE capacity when Hammersmith effects lowered over time, but they are still powered and present. Pax for example erupted during \u201ccore\u201d.<br /> <br /> By the way, during Aberrant era, Psiads would be called Novas, as well as more overt Talents. They would be Dark Stars (some one even said they are the ones called Dark Stars, because they are not detected by quantum sensors, but still have powers).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with this, with just one nitpick: stalwarts and mesmerists aren't in the core book. But retroactively, you can say that they are in the core books setting. Just in such limited supply that no one notices them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T08:22:13-07:00","id":1447200,"title":"","content":"So I thought the Doyen barrier basically just stopped the shenanigans' on Earth from going out into the wider universe rather than also limiting the potential of humanity inside said barrier. Now I am fine with this effect causing a limitation in Nova and Psiad (the book says psion which is technically wrong but whatever) but I am not a fan of this being what causes the manifestation of Stalwarts and Mesmerists. Basically I much prefer the idea that Stalwarts and Mesmerists came about due to Hammersmith only effecting miniscule fractions of psi and quantum and thus they came about due to human action and not alien limitations. Even unintentional ones. <br /> <br /> I do not want Stalwarts and Mesmerists to owe their existence due to Doyen plotting. <br /> <br /> Also, for me, Stalwarts and Mesmerists are something that can and does exist throughout human existence - all thanks to the timey whimey nature of the Hammersmith Event. So instead of automatically assuming its Novas or PSIADS!!! in the past or future one can also say it might be the Inspired. <br /> <br /> By the way the whole 'as the Hammersmith event fades away the Inspired loose access to their abilities' is not mentioned anywhere. A Stalwart is a Stalwart (unless they become a Nova) and a Mesmerist is a Mesmerist (unless they become a PSIAD) till they die - be it early through violence or after a normal human lifespan or even centuries later if they have slow aging or semi-immortality. The idea that suddenly one day a Stalwart wakes up and looses their powers just doesn't really work. <br /> <br /> I will say this - I am sooooo glad that this edition is a Continuum. That way its quite easy to make changes and be like &quot;oh yeah, its a different world than canon, though its similar enough in most ways&quot; and then throw some shinnanagians and have someone or something from canon arrive into the campaign world, or vis versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T08:32:56-07:00","id":1447202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447187#post1447187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) This goes against Aberrant Canon, because C.Pax was a naturally erupted Nova before N-Day, and Divis Mal also (that's why he was powerful enough to break the barrier in the first place). If my memory is right, Scripture was also a pre-N-Day Nova.<br /> <br /> How to reconcile all these?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I don't know about Pax, but for Mal and Scripture I had a theory that the first use of the Chrysalis was to filter out the (temporal) Flux in a Stalwart's body and gather enough Quantum Energy together for them to gain the first dot of Quantum, thus making them Novas. It would help explain how they would able to be Novas before the Doyen Barrier broke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T08:54:53-07:00","id":1447207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447200#post1447200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I thought the Doyen barrier basically just stopped the shenanigans' on Earth from going out into the wider universe rather than also limiting the potential of humanity inside said barrier. Now I am fine with this effect causing a limitation in Nova and Psiad (the book says psion which is technically wrong but whatever) but I am not a fan of this being what causes the manifestation of Stalwarts and Mesmerists. Basically I much prefer the idea that Stalwarts and Mesmerists came about due to Hammersmith only effecting miniscule fractions of psi and quantum and thus they came about due to human action and not alien limitations. Even unintentional ones. <br /> <br /> I do not want Stalwarts and Mesmerists to owe their existence due to Doyen plotting. <br /> <br /> Also, for me, Stalwarts and Mesmerists are something that can and does exist throughout human existence - all thanks to the timey whimey nature of the Hammersmith Event. So instead of automatically assuming its Novas or PSIADS!!! in the past or future one can also say it might be the Inspired. <br /> <br /> By the way the whole 'as the Hammersmith event fades away the Inspired loose access to their abilities' is not mentioned anywhere. A Stalwart is a Stalwart (unless they become a Nova) and a Mesmerist is a Mesmerist (unless they become a PSIAD) till they die - be it early through violence or after a normal human lifespan or even centuries later if they have slow aging or semi-immortality. The idea that suddenly one day a Stalwart wakes up and looses their powers just doesn't really work. <br /> <br /> I will say this - I am sooooo glad that this edition is a Continuum. That way its quite easy to make changes and be like &amp;quot;oh yeah, its a different world than canon, though its similar enough in most ways&amp;quot; and then throw some shinnanagians and have someone or something from canon arrive into the campaign world, or vis versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, there's no purpose to the doyen barrier storywise, as the closest thing that happens to anyone leaving Earth while it is up is the Moon landing. And if you want to allow for Pulp-style Mars and Venus, you can say that the barrier encompassed the inner solar system and not just Earth. So \u201ckeeps the energies from leaking out\u201d is more or less pointless. I had always wondered why the doyen barrier had been added to the setting, given that; with the reveal that it's is responsible for the differences between stalwart and Nova, it makes sense to have it.<br /> <br /> The fading of abilities over time is alluded to when it mentions that daredevils have more effective dramatic editing during the adventure era than the Talents that come after. It has not yet been confirmed that stalwarts and mesmerists lose access to dramatic editing over time; but it's a reasonable assumption to make given the daredevils versus Talents situation.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I agree about the benefits of it being a Continuum instead of the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:07:12-07:00","id":1447209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447207#post1447207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, there's no purpose to the doyen barrier storywise, as the closest thing that happens to anyone leaving Earth while it is up is the Moon landing. And if you want to allow for Pulp-style Mars and Venus, you can say that the barrier encompassed the inner solar system and not just Earth. So \u201ckeeps the energies from leaking out\u201d is more or less pointless. I had always wondered why the doyen barrier had been added to the setting, given that; with the reveal that it's is responsible for the differences between stalwart and Nova, it makes sense to have it.<br /> <br /> The fading of abilities over time is alluded to when it mentions that daredevils have more effective dramatic editing during the adventure era than the Talents that come after. It has not yet been confirmed that stalwarts and mesmerists lose access to dramatic editing over time; but it's a reasonable assumption to make given the daredevils versus Talents situation.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I agree about the benefits of it being a Continuum instead of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One could also have the Doyen barrier be a &quot;lock&quot; on humanity rather than around the planet/solar system. Much like the locked potential imposed on the Qin to keep them from ascending. Mal's &quot;break out&quot; might have been more of an alteration of this lock rather than breaking through a noetic bubble.<br /> <br /> And the Doyen &quot;lock&quot; may not be a bad thing. It may allow for maturity to settle into mankind before cosmic power ensues. Talents alone will get out into the cosmos given time. It may even be the best bet. <br /> <br /> For my tastes, I would treat Mal's ascension being a disaster for humanity. Sure, Novas are powerful, but the removal of the Flux and Psi aspects from Telluric Energy is apparently too much for most of them. Without those &quot;bumpers&quot; keeping Quantum corralled, most degenerate into monsters.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-03-2021, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T09:45:37-07:00","id":1447219,"title":"","content":"The advantage of the Doyen barrier explanation is that the result isn't strictly a limitation. An unintended consequence was that it didn't just suppress the telluric energies; for lack of a better term, it \u201ccompressed\u201d them, too. The manuscript describes how a Quantum particle and a Psi particle are connected through a Flux bond. My working theory, which is based on the WoG statement that the Doyen barrier changed how telluric energies interact, is that the barrier forced these particle bondings to strengthen. This manifests as the three types of Inspired being more alike during the Adventure era, and in the Quantum- and Psi-empowered humans having access to narrative-style Dramatic Editing. <br /> <br /> That, and it doesn't involve the Doyen tinkering with humanity itself. A stalwart <i>is</i> a Nova, having the M-R Coils; he's just a Nova that's operating in the unique environment caused by the Doyen barrier. A mesmerist <i>is</i> a psiad, genetically; she's just operating in the unique environment caused by the Doyen barrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:04:49-07:00","id":1447223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447219#post1447219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advantage of the Doyen barrier explanation is that the result isn't strictly a limitation. An unintended consequence was that it didn't just suppress the telluric energies; for lack of a better term, it \u201ccompressed\u201d them, too. The manuscript describes how a Quantum particle and a Psi particle are connected through a Flux bond. My working theory, which is based on the WoG statement that the Doyen barrier changed how telluric energies interact, is that the barrier forced these particle bondings to strengthen. This manifests as the three types of Inspired being more alike during the Adventure era, and in the Quantum- and Psi-empowered humans having access to narrative-style Dramatic Editing.<br /> <br /> That, and it doesn't involve the Doyen tinkering with humanity itself. A stalwart <i>is</i> a Nova, having the M-R Coils; he's just a Nova that's operating in the unique environment caused by the Doyen barrier. A mesmerist <i>is</i> a psiad, genetically; she's just operating in the unique environment caused by the Doyen barrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>That compressing is how it works in my head, too. It makes sense that the Doyen just wanted to keep the raw Telluric energy floating out there. They are quite aware of noetic energy and quantum energy but there is that &quot;weird&quot; bit there. So, they would just wall it all off. They can come back to it later. And, oh look, one of the humans broke the barrier. The Doyen now have to go back and deal with things. But...they do need to wait for all that quantum energy to die down a wee bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T10:20:54-07:00","id":1447227,"title":"","content":"Note that the point when they came back was when SK triggered her Event. I'm guessing that the way she cleared out so much of the quantum energy gave them a chance to come in and do their thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T11:29:38-07:00","id":1447241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1446429-\u00e6on-stalwarts-in-\u00e6on-trinity-and-superior-powers?p=1447219#post1447219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advantage of the Doyen barrier explanation is that the result isn't strictly a limitation. An unintended consequence was that it didn't just suppress the telluric energies; for lack of a better term, it \u201ccompressed\u201d them, too. The manuscript describes how a Quantum particle and a Psi particle are connected through a Flux bond. My working theory, which is based on the WoG statement that the Doyen barrier changed how telluric energies interact, is that the barrier forced these particle bondings to strengthen. This manifests as the three types of Inspired being more alike during the Adventure era, and in the Quantum- and Psi-empowered humans having access to narrative-style Dramatic Editing.<br /> <br /> That, and it doesn't involve the Doyen tinkering with humanity itself. A stalwart <i>is</i> a Nova, having the M-R Coils; he's just a Nova that's operating in the unique environment caused by the Doyen barrier. A mesmerist <i>is</i> a psiad, genetically; she's just operating in the unique environment caused by the Doyen barrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s was the intention, but as I see, all the explanation in first paragraph is perfect. In one of the books, not sure which, probably Aeon, the barrier is described as holding energies from have a large scale impact, so something like Hammersmith would not happen again, because nothing bigger than a city would be affected, no matter what. It would make the powers be limited somehow the same way, so a Nova or a Psiad would be capable of train and develop powers, but it would be like if they were bounded somehow, so they are making much more effort to achieve the same scale they would if not by the barrier. Once the barrier was broken, it was like if they were all freed and their powers just become more potent.<br /> <br /> I would add the \u201ccompressing\u201d made powers harder to use, but allowed them to take some control over Flux, what would not happen latter, so they are capable of limited (high cost) dramatic editing.<br /> <br /> Edit: A small comment, I would say DE is possible because the \u201ccompressing\u201d and because a high level in the Flux field, so basically the reality barriers are low. In Core, even with the \u201ccompressing\u201d still up, they would loose DE because of lower Flux field level (stronger reality barriers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-03-2021, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}